# 8. Phase F — Content Indexing and Synchronization

The earlier server implementation triggered full content indexing during application startup.

This is not an appropriate default for production.

## Required changes

Remove automatic full indexing from ordinary server startup.

Implement a controlled indexing lifecycle.

```text
Content created or updated
          ↓
Content published
          ↓
Indexing job scheduled
          ↓
Content normalized
          ↓
Chunks generated
          ↓
Embeddings generated
          ↓
Search index updated
          ↓
Tovu retrieval updated
```

Support:

- New content
- Updated content
- Republished content
- Archived content
- Deleted content
- Changed relationships

Ensure unpublished content cannot remain exposed through stale public embeddings or search results.

Use deterministic chunk identifiers where practical.

Make indexing idempotent.

Avoid regenerating embeddings for unchanged content.

Provide a restricted manual reindex operation.

If no production job infrastructure exists, implement the smallest reliable solution supported by the deployment environment and document its limitations.

Do not introduce a complex queue system without justification.

